{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/95112-an-idea-concept-or-reflection-regarding-the-ivory-claws","id":95112,"title":"An idea, concept or reflection regarding the Ivory Claws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-20T12:00:27-07:00","id":95112,"title":"An idea, concept or reflection regarding the Ivory Claws","content":"Ok, so something struck me regarding the Ivory Claws as an idea. I could of course be very wrong but I thought that I should throw it out.<br /> <br /> If I've understood the Ivroy Claws they are all about lineage and less about the individual than, say the Predator Kings, and thus I had an idea.<br /> <br /> What if the Ivory Claws, or at least some ancient and esteemed lineages, had an approach where they kind of strip away individuality from their members in favor of the traits associatied with the lineage? Using the normal Pure procedures they would then seek to eradicate traits that goes against what is &quot;normal&quot; for the lineage and magnify traits that are in accordance with their perception of the lineage. This attack on individuality is something which I wonder if it could have some merit in stories? As well as show how the Pure gives up much of themselves in their persuits.<br /> <br /> Themes that I can imagine are the weight of traditions, being proud of one's background, living in the shadows of the forefathers, never measuring up to the expected etc.<br /> <br /> That didn't come out all that good, but I'll give it a shot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T12:18:39-07:00","id":95129,"title":"","content":"Two words for you: Ancestor Spirits. Look them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:51:07-07:00","id":95190,"title":"","content":"I could see some ivory claw rite allowing an ancestor spirit to ride them and ride them until they're completely disassociated from their own identity.<br /> Better yet, a gift tree. I'd certainly love to see one. Perhaps it would fit into a lodge better, as it doesn't seem like an idea everyone would go for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-20-2014, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T14:08:14-07:00","id":96529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/95112-an-idea-concept-or-reflection-regarding-the-ivory-claws?p=95129#post95129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two words for you: Ancestor Spirits. Look them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know about Ancestor Spirits and its a good source of stuff that can be added to drive home the Ivory Claws' obsession with lineage but I was hoping for some other kind of input.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/95112-an-idea-concept-or-reflection-regarding-the-ivory-claws?p=95190#post95190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see some ivory claw rite allowing an ancestor spirit to ride them and ride them until they're completely disassociated from their own identity.<br /> Better yet, a gift tree. I'd certainly love to see one. Perhaps it would fit into a lodge better, as it doesn't seem like an idea everyone would go for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea about being ridden by an Ancestor Spirit to enhance one's ties to the lineage's supposed nature. I could see a lodge but I also kind of like the idea that it is a kind of thing within the tribe that is looked up on as a form of purification of oneself. Food for thought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}